# Rust build output
target/
# the same path as a SYMLINK. `scripts/shared-build-cache.sh` points this workspace's
# target/ at ONE cache every checkout on the machine shares, exactly as `src-tauri/target`
# below has been pointed at the external volume since 2026-09-17; a trailing-slash rule
# matches directories only, so the link would otherwise show as untracked.
/target

# `Cargo.lock` IS TRACKED — do not add an ignore rule for it.
#
# This file ignored every lockfile until 2026-09-04, which meant nobody could
# reproduce a build of RichOS: a fresh clone resolved 108 packages in the app
# workspace and 500 in the Tauri workspace to whatever compatible versions
# happened to be current that day. That is a nuisance for a library and a
# defect for an application, because an application is the thing whose exact
# dependency graph gets shipped.
#
# It also blocked the legal work. `docs/legal/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` makes a
# per-package dependency-license inventory a GATE on distributing a binary,
# and an inventory keyed to versions nobody can reproduce is not evidence — it
# is a document that looks like evidence. The lockfiles are what the inventory
# is keyed to.
#
# Both are committed: `app/Cargo.lock` and `app/src-tauri/Cargo.lock`. They are
# separate files because `src-tauri/` is a deliberately detached workspace (see
# the comment at the top of `app/Cargo.toml`), so Cargo resolves the two trees
# independently and there is no single lockfile that could cover both.

# The ACP adapter is GONE (wiki/ceo-decisions.md §16, 2026-08-31). This rule is kept for one
# release so a stale checkout that still has the directory does not commit its node_modules;
# there is no npm in the shipped app any more.
acp-adapter/node_modules/

# Tauri build / node UI deps
src-tauri/target/
# the same path as a SYMLINK (build cache relocated to the external SSD, 2026-09-17): a
# trailing-slash rule matches directories only, so the link would show as untracked
src-tauri/target
ui/node_modules/
ui/tests/node_modules/

# The SHIPPED frontend, staged from `ui/` by src-tauri/build.rs on every build.
#
# Generated, never authored: `ui/` is the source tree and holds both the product and the
# committed Playwright evidence under `ui/tests/`; this is the subset Tauri embeds into the
# binary. Committing it would put a second, drifting copy of every UI file in the repository
# and double the diff on every UI change.
ui-dist/

# Tauri-generated schemas (regenerated by tauri-build)
src-tauri/gen/

# RichDoctor (crates/richdoctor): the app's faces and token blocks, copied from ui/ by its build.rs on
# every build so RichDoctor ships the app's own files, never a second authored copy; and the
# schemas tauri-build regenerates.
crates/richdoctor/ui/fonts/
crates/richdoctor/ui/tokens.css
crates/richdoctor/gen/
